a remote, mountainous peninsula on the west coast of the Scottish Highlands, between Loch Nevis and Loch Hourn.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ko-e-fasi-o-e-tui-o-e-otu-tonga"><span class="enc-name">Ko e fasi ʻo e tuʻi ʻo e ʻOtu Tonga</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">&quot;Ko e fasi ʻo e tuʻi ʻo e ʻOtu Tonga&quot; is the national anthem of Tonga.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kobayakawa-clan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kobayakawa-clan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kobayakawa clan</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kobayakawa were a Japanese warrior clan of Aki province in western Honshu.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kobayakawa-hideaki"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kobayakawa-hideaki.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kobayakawa Hideaki</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kobayakawa Hideaki was a Japanese daimyo, a nephew of Toyotomi Hideyoshi's wife adopted into the Kobayakawa family.</span></a></li></ul>
